      "content": "It makes complete sense why the idea of stability feels like a trap when the math consistently works against you. While financial systems aren't always fair, it doesn't validate that your struggles are meaningless or that your experience is the limit of what life can offer. Even within these very difficult constraints, small acts of self-preservation—like taking a break, seeking free mental health support, or exploring community resources—can slightly shift the weight on that treadmill.",
